# What this repository does NOT hold.
#
# It used to exclude every vendored tree — `ainar-node/`, `ainar/`, `golden/`,
# `.agents/skills/`, `datalayer/` and three of the four plugins — on the ground
# that they were copies rather than source. That meant a fresh clone was not a
# working host: it needed `python -m exo setup` and a manual copy of two sibling
# checkouts, and the harness could not start until both had run.
#
# They are all tracked now, and as of 2026-09-08 they are not copies either:
# nothing outside this repository writes into it, and `PROVENANCE.md` records
# where each tree originally came from. Excluding them never protected anything —
# it only made the repository unusable on its own.
#
# Without their node_modules the whole set is about six megabytes.

# The credential file. `.env.example` is the tracked one.
.env
.env.local

# Installed dependencies and build output: reproducible from the manifests, and
# 147 MB across ainar-node and professor-skills.
node_modules/
dist/

# The harness's own state: sessions, credentials, whatever a profile installs
# beside itself. The profile DEFINITIONS under .dsh/profiles/*/ are tracked —
# they are the source of how this host is composed — and so are the agent
# presets under .dsh/.agent-presets/. Everything dsh writes next to them is not.
.dsh/sessions/
.dsh/storages/
.dsh/profiles/*/node_modules/
.dsh/.credentials*
.dsh/settings*

# Per-machine telemetry id, written by dsh at boot.
.dsh/.anonymous-user-id

# Python bytecode. There is no Python in this repository — `ainar/` is carried
# for its widget assets alone — so anything matching these got here by someone
# running an interpreter over a sibling checkout from inside this directory.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Editor and OS litter.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Rendered decks, and the scratch directories that build them.
#
# `pres render` writes to `<cwd>/output` by default, so decks built from this
# checkout land inside it. Slides are the one output that reliably carries
# things this repository must not publish — a draft argument, an unannounced
# result, a photograph, a student's work quoted as an example — and unlike the
# roster there is no code refusing to write them here. So the directory is
# excluded, and the decks this project has already produced were moved to
# `..\ProfessorExoskeleton-decks\` rather than left one `git add -A` from
# publication.
#
# To keep a deck out of reach entirely, render with an explicit destination
# outside the checkout: `pres render DECK.md --out-dir ..\ProfessorExoskeleton-decks`.
output/
.codex-build/
.codex-finalizer/

# The deployment's own user table: which professor listens on which port. It
# names real people on a real machine, which is a fact about that machine and
# not about this project. `deploy/users.conf.example` is the tracked one.
deploy/users.conf
